        "text": "(A typing office. Several clerks are there. Kumudha is typing. The manager, after looking over all the desks, comes and stands behind her. Kumudha is typing the same word over and over: 'Pandiyan, Pandiyan.')",
        "notes": []
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s061-u002",
        "kind": "dialogue",
        "speakerLabel": "மேனேஜர்",
        "sourceRecordId": "tirumbippaar-s061-d001",
        "sourceOccurrenceId": null,
        "pageProvenance": [
          {
            "pdfPage": 79,
            "printedPage": 71
          }
        ],
        "text": "Very neat indeed—what fine typing!",
        "notes": [
          "The manager's line is sarcastic in context; the translation preserves that tone rather than treating it as literal praise."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "tirumbippaar-en-s061-u003",
